> would insure that pressure would be applied uniformly to the radioactive
> material.  Correct me if I'm wrong.

I don't think this would work.  To trigger a fission bomb, you need
high explosives; "pressure" is an everyday concept that doesn't work
well in that sort of regime.  What you have is a set of shock waves,
the timing of whose reaching the fissionable material must be exact.
Too far off, and imbalanced shock wave will simply blow your scarce
plutonium all over the place.  Given the general rad hysteria, this
might not be that bad for the terrorist, but there are certainly
cheaper toxic materials.

